sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ha09-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The fishing-frog (angler) has long thin filaments with rounded tips in front of its eyes which it raises as bait while hidden in sand and mud, drawing small fish that touch them into its mouth.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The fishing-frog lures prey with filaments in front of its eyes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, The History of Animals (Historia Animalium), Book IX, Part 37; translated by D'Arcy Wentworth Thompson, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. IV (1910). Scope: fishing-frog (anglerfish, Lophius)"
}
